## Setup

Needs [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/). uv installs the Python version in
`.python-version`.

```bash
git init                      # if not already a git repo
uv lock                       # first time only, then commit uv.lock
uv sync                       # create .venv with all dev tools
uv run pre-commit install     # run fast checks on every commit
cp .env.example .env          # then fill in values
git add -A                    # hooks only check files git tracks
uv run poe check
```

## Everyday commands

| Command               | What it does                               |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `uv run poe check`    | Everything CI runs, in order               |
| `uv run poe lint`     | Pre-commit hooks on all files              |
| `uv run poe types`    | mypy strict                                |
| `uv run poe test`     | pytest with coverage (fails under 80%), skips integration tests |
| `uv run poe test-integration` | Tests marked `@pytest.mark.integration` (need network or credentials) |
| `uv run poe review`   | sp-repo-review against the Scientific Python guide |

## Layout

```text
src/{{ package_name }}/
  config.py          typed settings from env vars and .env
  errors.py          ProjectError base class and subclasses
  logging_setup.py   configure_logging() for entry points
tests/               pytest
docs/decisions/      decision records (NNNN-title.md)
```

## Standards

| Practice              | Standard                                   | Enforced by                     |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- |
| Project layout        | Scientific Python development guide        | `sp-repo-review` in CI          |
| Dependencies          | uv with a committed `uv.lock`              | `uv sync --locked` in CI        |
| Lint and format       | Ruff, including security rules (`S`)       | pre-commit and CI               |
| Types                 | mypy strict                                | pre-commit and CI               |
| Tests                 | pytest, coverage at least 80%              | CI                              |
| Docs and prose        | Markdown structure, no buzzwords or filler | pymarkdown and Vale             |
| Secrets               | `.env` only, never in code                 | detect-secrets (commit), TruffleHog (CI), GitHub push protection |
| Workflow security     | zizmor audit of GitHub Actions             | pre-commit and CI               |
| Dependency updates    | Dependabot, weekly, 7-day cooldown         | GitHub                          |
| Decisions             | Decision records in `docs/decisions/`      | Review                          |

## Decision records

Record each significant choice, and every departure from a standard, in
`docs/decisions/NNNN-title.md`. See
[0000](docs/decisions/0000-record-architecture-decisions.md) for the format.

